; The things lying in the world: their places
;
; Two bytes for each of the 290 objects, in the same order as map_object_kinds.
; Their column is the one map_objects_per_column puts them in; these give the
; rest, as spawn_objects_from_list unpacks them into an object slot.
;
; First byte: bits 2-7, less 1, the y within the map cell (slot +5); bits 0-1
; are bits 3-4 of the x within the cell. Second byte: bits 5-7 are bits 5-7 of
; the x (slot +2), and bits 0-4 the map row, 1-28 (slot +4). An object is put
; into a slot only when its row is the screen's map row or the one below.
;
; So objects are placed on an 8-unit grid in x and a 4-unit grid in y within
; their cell. Laid out below a line per map column, each object's kind (from
; map_object_kinds), row and place decoded, from the game's bytes when the
; disassembly is built.
