; The landscape tiles' records
;
; Each tile is drawn by draw_landscape as a list of pieces of ground, each a
; line of steps of one piece graphic. A record:
;
; Up to three optional markers first. $99: upside down -- floors become
; ceilings: each piece's direction is swapped through the second half of the
; table at mirror_table (0 and 7, 1 and 8 ... 6 and 13 swap places, 14 and 15
; swap), its y is turned over (XOR $0C) and its extra bytes XOR 1. $FF:
; mirrored left-right -- each piece's x is reflected, its two extra bytes are
; swapped (XOR 2) and its direction turned round through the table's first
; half. Then any byte of $95 or more is padding, skipped. Then the number of
; pieces; a record that is just 0 has none.
;
; Each piece: its x and y in the page; a byte with the direction in bits 4-7
; and the number of steps in bits 0-3 (0 means 16); and, only for directions 0
; and 7, two extra bytes (piece_extra_a, piece_extra_b). The direction picks
; three bytes from piece_shapes by set_piece_shape: the step in x, the step in
; y, and a third that is 0 for directions 0 and 7 (the flat pieces) and 8 or 16
; for the others. Directions 7 to 13 are the ceiling shapes of 0 to 6 and use
; the entry seven less, with piece_ceiling set.
;
; The padding rule is what lets four tiles share a record: a plain record of n
; pieces at A can be preceded by $99 (A-1, upside down), $FF $99 (A-2, mirrored
; left-right: the $99 is padding) and $99 $FF $99 (A-3, both). So 72 records,
; one after another with nothing between, serve all 171 tiles: 74 tiles have no
; marker, 27 are upside down, 51 mirrored left-right and 19 both. Read in
; Python, every byte from here to the tune is used except one (an unused $99,
; the third byte of the block).
;
; Laid out below a line per record, from the game's bytes when the disassembly
; is built: each marker a byte of its own, so that every tile's word in
; tile_table lands on one, then the count and the pieces; the comment names the
; tiles that read the record, and how, and decodes each piece as its (x,y) in
; the page, its direction and its steps, and a flat piece's two end codes.
tile_records:
  DEFB $00                ; Tiles $00, $20 and $2A. No pieces
  DEFB $00                ; Tile $A6. No pieces
  DEFB $99                ; Tile $5A (the marker $99 at its start is read by no
  DEFB $04                ; tile). 4 pieces: (8,63) direction 9 x 5 steps;
  DEFB $08,$3F,$95        ; (224,63) direction 12 x 5 steps; (40,183) direction
